WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.620
It's a new day on Tesla's short time, daily, episode 471, coming to you from Vancouver.

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:10.460
It's May 13th, 2026.

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:14.380
Tesla never sleeps, and neither does the new cycle.

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:21.980
Tesla's first use of Canada's new China EV tariff deal brings Shanghai Model 3's to market

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:24.300
at half the price of US-built versions.

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:32.240
Tesla's offering Shanghai-built Model 3 sedans in Canada for $C39,490.

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:39.580
That price sits well below the C-79,990 charge for the Fremont version.

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:48.840
The move follows a January trade deal that lowered tariffs on Chinese EVs from 100% to 6.1%,

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:51.880
under a quota of 49,000 vehicles.

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:56.680
Tesla becomes the first automaker to take advantage of the arrangement,

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:01.020
which also opens the door for competitors like BYD.

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:04.900
Now, shifting to the manufacturing side in Germany,

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:11.800
Tesla's Berlin Gigafactory has secured an additional $250 million in investment.

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:17.380
The funding ties directly to its fast hiring push and ongoing expansion.

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:22.880
Vehicle profits continue to support the broader robotics and AI plans.

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:29.500
This keeps the German site central to scaling both current production and future hardware ambitions.

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:32.720
Turning to software availability in Europe.

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:38.340
Tesla removed the basic autopilot option for new buyers in the Netherlands.

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:43.840
Only the paid, full-self driving package remains available for assisted driving.

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:49.160
The change aligns with efforts to monetize software more aggressively in Europe.

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:53.440
It raises questions about access for price-sensitive buyers.

00:01:54.340 --> 00:01:59.360
Owners shared footage of a cyber truck driving through standing water without issues.

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:05.780
The clip highlights the truck's high-ground clearance and sealed battery design in real conditions.

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:11.080
A post also showed a cyber truck on the Hawaiian island of Kauai.

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:16.560
The image underscores the truck's growing presence in non-traditional markets.

00:02:17.380 --> 00:02:21.300
Tesla filed a patent for a self-locking NASCS adapter.

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:26.960
The design prevents theft or loss once attached to non-Tesla vehicles.

00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:32.540
It addresses growing friction as a more third-party EVs adopt the connector.

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:38.380
Tesla introduced new financing options in China aimed at price-sensitive customers.

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:43.900
The moves follow Tesla falling out of the country's top-10 EV sellers.

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:48.180
They come just before a high-profile US-China visit.

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:55.000
The focus stays on stabilizing domestic volume while robotaxi and AI efforts continue.

00:02:55.780 --> 00:03:02.520
A driver born without arms shared how FSD supervised in a model Y reduced physical strain.

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:08.900
The system now handles steering and pedals that previously required awkward foot-only positioning.

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:14.860
Tesla shared the account to show practical accessibility benefits beyond performance claims.

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:21.640
Tesla posted a direct link encouraging drivers to schedule an FSD supervised demo.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:28.420
The message points to the company's ongoing push to get more owners behind the wheel of the supervised

00:03:28.420 --> 00:03:35.180
system. There is a challenge worth discussing with the removal of basic autopilot in the Netherlands.

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:41.820
The decision forces buyers who want any driver assistance to purchase the full package.

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:46.700
It tightens the gap between basic safety features and paid autonomy.

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:51.300
This could slow adoption among price-sensitive European customers.

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:56.820
Regulators may view the move as limiting access to proven safety technology.

00:03:57.540 --> 00:04:02.980
Taking a step back, the sudden availability of Shanghai-built Model 3s in Canada

00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:09.200
challenges the assumption that domestic assembly always protects local pricing power.

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:18.140
The 6.1% tariff now applied to a quota of 49,000 vehicles creates a direct cost gap of roughly

00:04:18.140 --> 00:04:27.000
$40,000,000 between otherwise identical cars. Trade policy can override manufacturing location

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:33.460
advantages in a single quarter. Tesla's vertical integration in Shanghai gives it the scale to

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:40.420
absorb shipping and compliance costs. The company will likely continue routing volume through whichever

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:47.540
plant faces the lowest effective barriers. Tomorrow, we'll be watching for how the new financing options

00:04:47.540 --> 00:04:55.480
perform in China and any further updates on FSD supervised demos. That's your Tesla news for today.

